When I first started working on the orchard, I thought it would be a breeze. I mean, how hard could it be, right? Just pick some apples, bag 'em up, and voila! But let me tell you, it was a whole different story. (note: this is an ongoing story and will be updated as more content is added)
At the orchard, we're kind of at the mercy of Mother Nature. Weather, pests, and diseases can all wreak havoc on our crops. So, we have to be super vigilant and ready to adapt at a moment's notice. Like, last week, we got hit with a nasty frost that killed off about a quarter of our apple crop. (note: this is an ongoing story and will be updated as more content is added)
